I'm John Ball this is my beautiful wife  when we live in San Antonio Texas and in  2015  I took a two thousand six hundred and  eighty three mile walk across the United  States beginning in San Diego California  and I finished my walk in Daytona Beach  Florida  [Music]  f/16 his buddies out there somewhere  brother wen and I got married very young  and after graduated from college I had  never been in an airplane never flown an  airplane I've never even bought a ticket  and ridden on an airplane and so I went  down to the recruiters office in our  hometown of Paris Texas and applied to  go to Air Force pilot training when Winn  was very supportive of that and off we  went to the Air Force 26 years later I  retired as a colonel having been a pilot  for most of that time including a  two-year stint as Air Force two pilot  for Vice President Gore and Vice  President Cheney  throughout my Air Force career I'd  always been an avid exerciser I'd go out  jogging 6 8 10 miles a day but towards  the end of my career I was approaching  50 years old my knees started hurting  pretty bad I went to the doctor the  doctor said you really need to lay off  the running for a while so I started  walking very the very next day I started  walking for exercise and I never stopped  walking so I was just honestly out  walking one day and it just crossed my  mind I wonder what it would be like to  walk a long distance  specifically I immediately came to my  mind what would it be like to walk all  the way across the country after I  retired from the Air Force I went to  work here in San Antonio with a  government contractor and at that point  when and I were able to live off of my  Air Force pension but we wanted to  rebuild our retirement home and here in  San Antonio with the exception of the  savings that we did we put everything  else towards paying off our retirement  home  after I retired I immediately started on  this walk the walk ended up being 2686  miles and 170 days from March 1st to  August 17th  well they're a couple couple of things  that I had to consider number one I had  to be in good enough health to be able  to walk that kind of distance it's  pretty grueling walking 270 days without  a lot of rest  the other thing is economically I had to  be able to do that and that all tied  into being debt-free we cash flowed the  entire trip and the purpose of the trip  was to create an endowed scholarship at  my alma mater Texas A&amp;M and because I  had prepared financially to be able to  go on the walk at my own cost all the  donations that came in went straight to  the scholarship there's a tradition at  Texas A&amp;M about the Aggie ring we've had  the same graduation ring for over a  hundred years and so really it's a it's  your tradition and it's a it's an honor  that all Aggies have to wear their Aggie  ring but not everybody can afford their  Aggie ring when it's time for them to to  get it 350 very generous people gave  over $27,000 to establish the walking  Aggie and doubt ring scholarship so that  each year one male student our two  female students receive their a green as  a result of the scholarship and my  completion of the coast-to-coast walk  I got more than my share of input from  people telling me that it was dangerous  that there are a lot of mean people out  there and that it was just generally a  bad idea to to go walking on my own  without any help or support for six  months I will tell you that that is the  one thing that I learned throughout this  walk was how kind people are in six  months I never had one single incident  where I felt threatened in any way by  anyone I walked into gas stations I  walked into cafes I was greeted on the  shoulder of the road with people  offering me rides and water and food the  the best experience out of the whole  trip was just how kind people were to me  there was a relief because as the family  we were very worried about his safety  and he just had a great experience  I had a very detailed plan for the walk  I knew where I was supposed to be every  day with that in mind we booked the  Disney cruise that left the afternoon of  August the 17th so I knew before I ever  started on March 1st in San Diego that I  had to be in Daytona Beach Florida on  August 17th or that cruise ship was  gonna leave without us  the whole family flew up to San Diego to  see mom and really comes back because we  were all together and about to go to  Disneyland and here he was all by  herself can walk away but anyway we  could talk every day just very seldom  did we not speak every day so we're  trying to kept up with Dean and knew  that he was okay it just all worked out  good and then we all went including my  mom on the other end and took a Disney  cruise so he better finish on time dead  free we were millionaires by then and  that just that just freed us up to be  able to really go out and live life the  way we had planned for a long time you  know we go to Europe and tulle around  Europe with our backpacks for weeks at a  time we have a goal we motorcycle with a  little trailer we pull over it behind it  we just got back from a trip to Canada  and then in April we're going to visit  Eastern Europe so we really like to  travel and being debt-free has enabled  us to do that and that was something we  always hopefully to do and and now we're  living in  being debt-free before I started this  walk it really enabled me to be able to  pull this off we saved our entire Air  Force career and we saved and we're able  to pay off our house and become  debt-free the month that I've started on  the walk and it really it really just  lived out the philosophy that if you  live like no one else you can live and  give like no one else  [Music]  [Music]
 

